Live measurement at 390x844 (iPhone 12/13/14/15 width), after sending one message:
{"vw":390,"brandName":[175,288],"brandSub":[102,167],"newChat":[16,119],"overlapPx":17,"parentWidth":149}
At 360x740: brandSub [72,167] vs newChat [16,119] → 47px overlap. The flex child holding <h1 class="brand-name"> + <span class="brand-sub"> has min-width:0 so it shrinks to 149px, but both children are `white-space: nowrap` (globals.css:986-987) and need ~186px, so they overflow into the button. globals.css:1030-1037 sets `.shell { overflow: hidden }`, so document.scrollWidth === clientWidth (hScroll:false) — the text is clipped/overlapped, never reachable. Visible in both captured screenshots as "…iara Copilotلگفت‌وگوی جدید". globals.css contains zero width-based media queries (`grep -n "@media"` returns only prefers-color-scheme, prefers-reduced-motion x3, min-height:700px, pointer:coarse).

Nine live turns against POST /api/chat. Per-turn (n = citations, numbered = citations carrying `n`, markers = [n] markers in the answer body):
{"q":"…Next.js…","n":5,"numbered":0,"markers":0}
{"q":"…PostgreSQL…","n":2,"numbered":2,"markers":4}
{"q":"…متغیرهای محیطی…","n":4,"numbered":4,"markers":4}
{"q":"…دامنه اختصاصی…","n":4,"numbered":0,"markers":0}
{"q":"…لاگ‌ها…","n":3,"numbered":0,"markers":0}
{"q":"…object storage…","n":1,"numbered":1,"markers":1}
plus "How do I deploy a Django app on Liara?" → n:3, markers:null, and two browser runs → markers:0.
When n is null, Markdown.tsx:99-101 builds an empty byN map so citationPlugin no-ops, and Sources.tsx:35 drops the [n] badge — the answer body has zero clickable per-claim links and the list is unnumbered. Sources.tsx:28 `open={citations.length <= 2 || undefined}` then leaves the 3–5-source case CLOSED: browser-verified three times, {"srcOpen":false,"srcN":3,"markers":0,"summary":"منابع (3)"}. Also 6 of 20 citation URLs carried no #:~:text= fragment, e.g. https://docs.liara.ir/paas/domains/about/ (HTTP 200, no highlight) — that click lands at the top of a long page.

Chat.tsx:146-149 sets maxLength={MAX_INPUT_CHARS} (8000) on the textarea. Live in Chrome: inserted a 14,100-character stack-trace-style log via document.execCommand('insertText') on the deployed page →
input chars 14100 {"pasted":8000,"maxLength":8000,"counter":"۸٬۰۰۰ از ۸٬۰۰۰ نویسه","sendDisabled":false}
6,100 characters are dropped with no toast, no error, no visual mark. The only signal is the character counter, which only appears above 7,200 chars (Chat.tsx:37 COUNTER_FROM) and reads "۸٬۰۰۰ از ۸٬۰۰۰ نویسه" — "8,000 of 8,000", which a user reads as "you're at the limit", not "we deleted the second half of your log". Send is enabled, so the truncated log — whose real error line is usually near the end — is submitted as if complete.
